<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>PSP TDS · waveform atlas</title>
<style>
:root{--ink:#17313d;--muted:#58707b;--accent:#007c91;--line:#d9e3e8;--paper:#f3f6f7}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:15px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}header{background:#143341;color:white;padding:28px 4vw 24px}header p{max-width:1000px;color:#c3d9df}h1{font-size:32px;margin:4px 0}h2{font-size:23px;margin:0 0 12px}h3{font-size:16px;margin:5px 0}p{margin:8px 0}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#90ced8}.wrap{max-width:1550px;padding:24px;margin:auto}.panel{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px}.muted{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:15px;margin-top:18px}.stat{border-left:2px solid #62b4c4;padding-left:15px}.stat b{font-size:25px;display:block}.stat span{font-size:13px;color:#c3d9df}.groups{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(215px,1fr));gap:12px}.card{border:1px solid var(--line);border-top:4px solid var(--accent);border-radius:6px;padding:12px}.card button{margin-top:8px}button,select,input,textarea{font:inherit;border:1px solid #b9cbd3;border-radius:5px;background:#fff;padding:6px 10px;color:var(--ink)}button{cursor:pointer;background:#edf5f7}button:hover{background:#d3e9ef}a{color:var(--accent)}.tools{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:end;margin:12px 0}.tools label{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:3px}select{max-width:240px}input[type=search]{width:270px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:360px minmax(0,1fr);gap:18px}.list{height:570px;overflow:auto;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px}th{position:sticky;top:0;background:#eef3f5;text-align:left}td,th{padding:7px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #e9eff1}tr[data-id]{cursor:pointer}tr.active{background:#d8edf2}tr[data-id]:hover{background:#edf5f7}.plotgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.45fr 1fr 1fr;gap:5px;min-width:780px}.plotscroll{overflow:auto}.chart{width:100%;height:125px;display:block}.plothead{text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);padding:4px}.eventmeta{background:#f4f7f8;border-radius:6px;padding:10px;font-size:13px;margin-bottom:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.badge{display:inline-block;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:12px;background:#e8f0f3;font-size:12px;margin-right:5px}.amber{background:#fff1d4;color:#785610}.legend{display:flex;gap:15px;font-size:12px;margin:5px 0;flex-wrap:wrap}#map{width:100%;height:290px;cursor:crosshair}.side h3{margin-top:15px}.eventtitle{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}.annotation{display:grid;grid-template-columns:200px 1fr auto;gap:8px}.annotation input,.annotation textarea{width:100%}.annotation textarea{height:55px}.overview{width:100%;height:auto}.details{max-width:1050px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;padding:5px 0}.loading{padding:50px;text-align:center;font-size:20px}#app{display:none}.note{padding:10px 12px;border-left:3px solid #d99a44;background:#fff8ea;font-size:13px}footer{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;padding:20px 0}@media(max-width:1000px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.list{height:240px}.stats{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.annotation{grid-template-columns:1fr}.wrap{padding:12px}}@media print{.tools,.side,.annotation,button{display:none}.grid{display:block}header{color:#17313d;background:white}.panel{break-inside:avoid}}
</style></head><body>
<header><div class="eyebrow">Parker Solar Probe · FIELDS / TDS + SWEAP SPAN-electron</div><h1>Waveform morphology atlas</h1><p><a style="color:#a8e7ef" href="methods.html#encounters">PSP encounter tags and date definitions</a></p><p>__DATES__ · An unsupervised first pass through __N__ TDS waveform bursts. Explore waveform shape, electron-count structure, and unusual events without assigning physical labels.</p><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><b>__N__</b><span>bursts · 17.07 ms each</span></div><div class="stat"><b>5 + 1</b><span>analog channels + digital counts</span></div><div class="stat"><b>__CORE__</b><span>analog core assignments</span></div><div class="stat"><b>__R2__</b><span>cross-day sweep-phase R² for log counts</span></div></div><p><a style="color:#a8e7ef;font-weight:600" href="methods.html">Analysis methods &amp; plot guide →</a></p></header>
<div id="loading" class="loading">Loading local waveform previews…<p class="muted">Unpacking the embedded dataset. No network connection is used.</p></div>
<main id="app" class="wrap">
<section class="panel"><h2>What emerged</h2><p><button data-pick="1584">Inspect dust-impact reference · Event 1584</button> <a href="methods.html#expert-labels">About user identifications</a></p><p>The analog partition separates several recurring morphologies, with substantial overlap: <b>__AMBIG__ ambiguous, __OUTLIERS__ outlier, __SAT__ saturated, and __CONFIG__ configuration-exception</b> records remain outside the core assignments. These are provisional browsing groups.</p><p>SPAN-electron counts have strong sweep-phase structure. Raw-count classes and analog classes organize the records differently; residual count groups after phase conditioning are less stable. Persistent narrow lines carry most of the SCM spectral power and affect the analog partition.</p><p><a href="electron_voltage_report.md">Electron–voltage correlations</a> · <a href="methods.html">Analysis methods &amp; plot guide</a> · <a href="event_catalog.csv" download>Download event catalog</a> · <a href="README.md">Reproduce the analysis</a></p><details><summary>Overview and stability checks</summary><img class="overview" src="data:image/png;base64,__OVERVIEW__" alt="Six-panel overview of analog groups, separation, count sweep-phase structure, selection types, and assignment status"><p class="muted">PCA is a projection for navigation; it contains only __PCAPERCENT__ of feature variance. Clustering uses all 89 features. The selected k = __K__ maximizes silhouette among candidate partitions with at least 20 records per group.</p></details></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Heliocentric distance</h2><p>The CDFs provide valid spacecraft-reported solar distance at every burst. These records span approximately __RANGE__ R☉. Distance and inbound/outbound direction are context only and were not used to form the groups.</p><details><summary>Show radial comparisons</summary><img class="overview" src="data:image/png;base64,__RADIALFIG__" alt="Radial distance through time, group mix by radius, analog amplitude and counts versus radius"></details></section><section class="panel"><h2>Provisional analog groups</h2><div id="groups" class="groups"></div><p class="muted">Parent-group counts include ambiguous/outlier members and exclude saturation and configuration exceptions. Names describe representative examples, not established physical populations.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Electron counts and voltage correlations</h2><p>Across-burst count/amplitude correlations are modest (Spearman __POOLR__) and change to __ADJR__ after adjustment for sweep phase, day, radius, selection, SWEAP status and TWTA flag. For the common V4 / SCM5 configuration, median within-burst envelope correlations are close to zero. Individual candidates have larger correlations, often involving slow trends; no physical coupling or precise delay is established.</p><details><summary>Population comparisons</summary><img class="overview" src="data:image/png;base64,__CORRFIG__" alt="Across-burst and within-burst count–voltage correlations"></details><p>Inspect candidates selected by peak residual correlation (at least 128 counts):</p><p>__CORRCARDS__</p>__CORRDETAIL__<p><a href="electron_voltage_report.md">Methods, native-cadence checks and trend sensitivity</a> · <a href="electron_voltage_correlations.csv" download>Per-burst coefficients</a></p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Alternate V5 / SCM4 configuration</h2><p>These records were analyzed separately. __ALTNOTE__ Their electron–voltage comparisons use the actual available channels.</p><p>__ALTCARDS__</p><details><summary>Alternate-configuration correlations</summary><img class="overview" src="data:image/png;base64,__ALTFIG__" alt="Electron-count and voltage correlations for V5 configuration"></details><p><a href="alternate_configuration_report.md">Separate analysis and methods</a> · <a href="alternate_voltage_correlations.csv">Per-event coefficients</a></p></section><section class="panel"><h2>SCM–voltage associations</h2><p>Each available voltage is compared with SCM5 or SCM4 using signed waveform correlation, RMS envelopes and spectral coherence. Flags are descriptive screening thresholds; they do not establish physical wave modes. Coherence outside learned persistent-line bins is retained separately from line-dominated coherence.</p><details><summary>SCM association overview</summary><img class="overview" src="data:image/png;base64,__SCMFIG__" alt="SCM/voltage association summary"></details><p>__SCMCARDS__</p>__SCMDETAIL__<p><a href="scm_voltage_report.md">Flag definitions and results</a> · <a href="scm_voltage_correlations.csv">All pairwise coefficients</a></p></section><section class="panel" id="explorer"><h2>Inspect all six channels</h2><div class="tools">
<label>SCM association<select id="scmflag"><option value="">All</option><option>waveform correlation</option><option>envelope association</option><option>coherence outside persistent lines</option><option>persistent-line dominated coherence</option><option>no threshold crossed</option><option>not assessed</option></select></label><label>Analog group<select id="group"><option value="">All groups</option></select></label><label>Alternate A group<select id="agroup"><option value="">All</option></select></label><label>Analog status<select id="status"><option value="">All statuses</option><option>core</option><option>ambiguous</option><option>outlier</option><option>saturated</option><option>alternate_configuration</option><option>incomplete</option></select></label>
<label>Count view<select id="cview"><option value="count_group">Raw-count groups C</option><option value="residual_count_group">Phase-residual groups R</option><option value="joint_group">Joint groups J</option></select></label><label>Count / joint group<select id="cgroup"><option value="">All</option></select></label>
<label>Encounter period<select id="encounter"><option value="">All periods</option><option value="within">Encounter dates</option><option value="before">Before encounter</option><option value="after">After encounter</option><option value="unassigned">Unassigned</option></select></label><label>Day<select id="day"><option value="">All days</option>__DAYOPTIONS__</select></label>
<label>Radius (R☉)<select id="radius"><option value="">All radii</option><option>9.5:12</option><option>12:15</option><option>15:18</option><option>18:21</option><option>21:24</option><option>24:27</option><option>27:30</option><option>30:40</option><option>40:50</option><option>50:60</option><option>60:80</option><option>80:100</option><option>100:120</option></select></label><label>Orbit leg<select id="leg"><option value="">Both legs</option><option>inbound</option><option>outbound</option></select></label><label>Search UTC, event or burst ID<input id="search" type="search" placeholder="e.g. 806 or 17:30"></label><label>Sort<select id="sort"><option value="time">Time</option><option value="pc1">Highest PC1</option><option value="impulse">Most impulsive first</option><option value="uncertain">Least stable first</option><option value="residual">Largest count residual first</option><option value="scmcoherence">Largest SCM coherence outside lines</option><option value="scmenvelope">Largest SCM envelope association</option><option value="correlation">Largest voltage/count residual correlation</option><option value="coupling">Largest envelope association first</option></select></label>
<button id="clear">Reset filters</button></div>
<div class="grid"><aside class="side"><div id="found" class="muted"></div><div class="list"><table><thead><tr><th>Event / UTC</th><th>Analog</th><th>Counts</th></tr></thead><tbody id="events"></tbody></table></div><h3>Analog morphology map</h3><p class="muted">PI interpretation: the high-PC1 population contains dust impacts. No numerical boundary has been assigned. Axis scores are dimensionless; colors still show unsupervised groups.</p><canvas id="map"></canvas><p class="muted">Click a point to inspect. Colors indicate G groups; black outlines mark the selected event. Only filtered records are shown.</p><h3>Nearest analog neighbors</h3><div id="neighbors"></div></aside>
<div><div class="eventtitle"><h3 id="title"></h3><div><button id="previous">← Previous</button> <button id="next">Next →</button></div></div><div id="meta" class="eventmeta"></div>
<div class="tools"><label>Analog y scaling<select id="scale"><option value="engineering">Engineering units</option><option value="rms">Divide by each channel RMS</option></select></label><a id="figure" target="_blank">Open full-resolution example PNG</a></div>
<p class="muted">Analog medians removed. Full-record plots preserve extrema in 256 display bins; their ripples are not resolved waveforms. Zooms show 512 actual consecutive samples at the strongest normalized electric excursion.</p>
<div class="plotscroll"><div class="plotgrid" id="plots"><div class="plothead">Full record · 17.07 ms</div><div class="plothead">Actual-sample zoom · 0.267 ms</div><div class="plothead">Welch PSD · dB re unit²/Hz</div></div></div>
<div class="legend"><span style="color:#222">━ SPAN-e observed counts / 66.67 µs</span><span style="color:#d86b25">━ Scan-pattern reference, scaled to this burst</span></div>
<canvas id="residual" style="width:100%;height:145px"></canvas><p class="muted">Count residual = (observed − scaled scan reference) / √(scaled scan reference + 1). The reference shape is learned from other days; its scale is fitted to this burst’s total counts, not an instrument gain. Unsupported status matches are flagged above. This normalization is not a calibrated noise estimate. <a href="methods.html#phase-baseline">How the reference is calculated</a>.</p>
<h3>SCM–voltage pair metrics</h3><p class="muted">Envelope lag is positive when SCM follows voltage. Coherence is a weighted average over 1–864 kHz. Outside-line peak frequency alone is not a detection.</p><div class="plotscroll" id="scmpairs"></div><h3>Optional review notes</h3><div class="annotation"><input id="label" placeholder="Your descriptive label"><textarea id="notes" placeholder="Observations, ambiguity, or an interpretation to revisit"></textarea><button id="save">Save locally</button></div><p class="muted" id="saved">Notes are stored in this browser. Export them to preserve a portable copy.</p><button id="export">Export annotations as JSON</button>
</div></div></section>
<section class="panel details"><h2>Reading the labels</h2><p><b>G:</b> analog parent groups, fitted on the common five-channel configuration without saturated events. __ALTNOTE__ Core requires silhouette ≥0.05 and ≥80% matched-label resampling agreement; those values are not classification probabilities. The __OUTLIERS__ outliers are selected by a 98th-percentile neighbor-distance rule.</p><p><b>C:</b> independent raw count-shape groups. __ZEROS__ bursts have no counts and __SPARSE__ have 1–31 counts; these remain unassigned.</p><p><b>R:</b> phase-residual count groups. <b>J:</b> an exploratory __K__-way joint partition on __JOINTN__ eligible records. Numbering is independent across G, C, R, and J. Group numbers can change after refitting; saved annotations retain stable event IDs.</p><p><b>Calibration:</b> these are engineering mV and nT. All frequency-response-corrected physical-unit flags are off. The digital stream is counts per sample. SWEAP status bits and selection masks are retained but not decoded.</p><p>Cross-channel envelope associations are candidates for inspection. Scan structure and nonstationarity can generate them; they are not identified wave–particle interactions. Onboard selection means the catalog represents recorded bursts, not unbiased occurrence rates.</p><p id="figpath" class="muted">Figure files: /Users/bale/Dropbox/projects/PSP/Work/TDS/figures/waveform_classification/</p></section>
<footer>Local, offline artifact · Original CDFs unchanged · Source hashes and complete numerical diagnostics accompany this atlas.</footer></main>
<script id="payload" type="application/octet-stream">__PAYLOAD__</script>
<script>
let DATA,rows,previews,filtered=[],current=0,annotations={},mapped=[];const colors=['#007c91','#d86b25','#7d4db0','#388a52','#bd4671','#a39520','#497dcc','#555555','#00a59b','#a0522d'];const channels=['V2','V4','V1−V2','V3−V4','SCM5','SPAN-e'];const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);const safe=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
function num(v,d=3){return v==null?'—':Number(v).toPrecision(d)}
function setupCanvas(canvas){let w=canvas.clientWidth||350,h=canvas.clientHeight||125;let ratio=devicePixelRatio||1;canvas.width=w*ratio;canvas.height=h*ratio;let ctx=canvas.getContext('2d');ctx.scale(ratio,ratio);ctx.clearRect(0,0,w,h);return {ctx,w,h}}
function chart(canvas,x,series,title,xlabel,ylabel,logx=false,band=null){let {ctx,w,h}=setupCanvas(canvas),left=57,right=8,top=22,bottom=27,pw=w-left-right,ph=h-top-bottom;let xx=logx?x.map(Math.log10):x;let xmin=xx[0],xmax=xx.at(-1);let values=series.flatMap(s=>s.y);if(band)values=values.concat(band.lo,band.hi);let ymin=Infinity,ymax=-Infinity;for(let v of values){if(Number.isFinite(v)){ymin=Math.min(ymin,v);ymax=Math.max(ymax,v)}}if(!Number.isFinite(ymin)){ymin=0;ymax=1}if(ymax===ymin){ymin-=.5;ymax+=.5}let pad=(ymax-ymin)*.06;ymin-=pad;ymax+=pad;const X=v=>left+(v-xmin)/(xmax-xmin||1)*pw,Y=v=>top+ph-(v-ymin)/(ymax-ymin)*ph;ctx.font='11px system-ui';ctx.fillStyle='#17313d';ctx.fillText(title,4,12);ctx.font='9px system-ui';for(let q=0;q<3;q++){let v=ymin+(ymax-ymin)*q/2,y=Y(v);ctx.strokeStyle='#e9eff2';ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(left,y);ctx.lineTo(w-right,y);ctx.stroke();ctx.fillStyle='#58707b';ctx.textAlign='right';ctx.fillText(num(v,2),left-4,y+3)}for(let q=0;q<3;q++){let v=xmin+(xmax-xmin)*q/2;ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText(num(logx?10**v:v,3),X(v),h-14)}ctx.save();ctx.beginPath();ctx.rect(left,top,pw,ph);ctx.clip();if(band){ctx.strokeStyle=band.color;ctx.lineWidth=.7;ctx.beginPath();band.lo.forEach((v,i)=>{ctx.moveTo(X(xx[i]),Y(v));ctx.lineTo(X(xx[i]),Y(band.hi[i]))});ctx.stroke()}for(let s of series){ctx.strokeStyle=s.color;ctx.lineWidth=s.width||1;ctx.beginPath();s.y.forEach((v,i)=>{if(i===0)ctx.moveTo(X(xx[i]),Y(v));else if(s.step){ctx.lineTo(X(xx[i]),Y(s.y[i-1]));ctx.lineTo(X(xx[i]),Y(v))}else ctx.lineTo(X(xx[i]),Y(v))});ctx.stroke()}ctx.restore();ctx.fillStyle='#58707b';ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText(xlabel,left+pw/2,h-2);ctx.textAlign='left';ctx.fillText(ylabel,left,top+9)}
function populateCountFilter(){let key=$('cview').value,groups=[...new Set(rows.map(r=>r[key]))].sort((a,b)=>a-b),prefix=key==='count_group'?'C':key==='residual_count_group'?'R':'J';$('cgroup').innerHTML='<option value="">All</option>'+groups.map(g=>`<option value="${g}">${g<0?'Unassigned / insufficient':prefix+g}</option>`).join('');filter()}
function filter(){let query=$('search').value.toLowerCase(),ck=$('cview').value;filtered=rows.filter(r=>(!$('encounter').value||r.encounter_period===$('encounter').value)&&(!$('scmflag').value||r.scm_voltage_flags.split('; ').includes($('scmflag').value))&&(!$('group').value||r.group===+$('group').value)&&(!$('agroup').value||r.alternate_group===+$('agroup').value)&&(!$('status').value||r.status===$('status').value)&&(!$('day').value||r.day===$('day').value)&&(!$('leg').value||r.radial_direction===$('leg').value)&&(!$('radius').value||(r.solar_distance_Rs>=+$('radius').value.split(':')[0]&&r.solar_distance_Rs<+$('radius').value.split(':')[1]))&&(!$('cgroup').value||r[ck]===+$('cgroup').value)&&(!query||String(r.event)===query||String(r.Burst_ID)===query||r.utc.toLowerCase().includes(query)||r.encounter_tag.toLowerCase().includes(query)||expertLabel(r).toLowerCase().includes(query)));let s=$('sort').value;filtered.sort((a,b)=>s==='pc1'?b.pc1-a.pc1:s==='impulse'?b.impulsiveness-a.impulsiveness:s==='uncertain'?(a.stability??-1)-(b.stability??-1):s==='residual'?b.counts_phase_residual_rms-a.counts_phase_residual_rms:s==='scmcoherence'?(b.scm_voltage_max_outside_line_coherence??-1)-(a.scm_voltage_max_outside_line_coherence??-1):s==='scmenvelope'?(b.scm_voltage_max_envelope_abs_r??-1)-(a.scm_voltage_max_envelope_abs_r??-1):s==='correlation'?(b.voltage_count_peak_abs_r??-1)-(a.voltage_count_peak_abs_r??-1):s==='coupling'?b.counts_envelope_max_abs_corr-a.counts_envelope_max_abs_corr:a.utc.localeCompare(b.utc));$('found').textContent=`${filtered.length} of ${rows.length} bursts`;renderList();drawMap();if(filtered.length&&!filtered.some(r=>r.event===current))select(filtered[0].event);else if(!filtered.length)$('found').textContent='No matches. Change or reset filters.'}
function renderList(){$('events').innerHTML=filtered.map(r=>`<tr data-id="${r.event}" class="${r.event===current?'active':''}"><td><b>${r.event}</b> · ${r.utc.slice(8,10)} Mar<br>${r.utc.slice(11,23)}</td><td><b style="color:${(colors[r.group]||'#999')}">${r.group<0?(r.alternate_group>=0?'A'+r.alternate_group:'Unassigned'):'G'+r.group}</b><br>${r.status}</td><td>${r.count_group<0?'—':'C'+r.count_group}<br>${r.counts_present===false?'channel absent':r.counts_total.toLocaleString()}</td></tr>`).join('')}
function drawMap(){if(!rows)return;let {ctx,w,h}=setupCanvas($('map'));let plotrows=rows.filter(r=>r.group>=0);if(!plotrows.length)return;let xmin=Math.min(...plotrows.map(r=>r.pc1))-.1,xmax=Math.max(...plotrows.map(r=>r.pc1))+.1,ymin=Math.min(...plotrows.map(r=>r.pc2))-.1,ymax=Math.max(...plotrows.map(r=>r.pc2))+.1;let left=52,right=w-18,top=32,bottom=h-45;let X=v=>left+(v-xmin)/(xmax-xmin)*(right-left),Y=v=>bottom-(v-ymin)/(ymax-ymin)*(bottom-top);ctx.font='11px system-ui';ctx.lineWidth=1;for(let k=0;k<=4;k++){let vx=xmin+(xmax-xmin)*k/4,vy=ymin+(ymax-ymin)*k/4;ctx.strokeStyle='#e0e7ea';ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(vx),top);ctx.lineTo(X(vx),bottom);ctx.moveTo(left,Y(vy));ctx.lineTo(right,Y(vy));ctx.stroke();ctx.fillStyle='#17313d';ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText(vx.toFixed(2),X(vx),bottom+16);ctx.textAlign='right';ctx.fillText(vy.toFixed(2),left-7,Y(vy)+4)}mapped=[];for(let r of filtered){if(r.group<0)continue;let x=X(r.pc1),y=Y(r.pc2);mapped.push([x,y,r.event]);ctx.globalAlpha=r.status==='core'?.65:.35;ctx.fillStyle=(colors[r.group]||'#999');ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(x,y,3,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fill()}ctx.globalAlpha=1;let r=rows[current];if(r&&r.group>=0){ctx.strokeStyle='#111';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(X(r.pc1),Y(r.pc2),6,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.stroke()}ctx.fillStyle='#17313d';ctx.font='12px system-ui';ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText('PC1 · '+(100*DATA.model.pca_explained[0]).toFixed(1)+'% variance',(left+right)/2,h-7);ctx.textAlign='left';ctx.fillText('PC2 · '+(100*DATA.model.pca_explained[1]).toFixed(1)+'% variance',left,14);ctx.textAlign='right';ctx.fillStyle='#905214';ctx.font='11px system-ui';ctx.fillText('High PC1: dust impacts (PI) →',right,top-4);ctx.textAlign='left'}
function expertLabel(r){return r.file==="psp_fld_l2_tds_wf_20250318_v00.cdf"&&Number(r.record)===56?"Dust impact · user-identified reference":""}
function select(i){current=+i;let r=rows[current],p=previews[current];$('title').textContent=`Event ${r.event} · ${r.utc.slice(0,26)} UTC`;$('meta').innerHTML=`<span class="badge ${r.status!=='core'?'amber':''}">${r.group<0?(r.alternate_group>=0?'A'+r.alternate_group:'Unassigned'):'G'+r.group} · ${r.status}${r.status==='saturated'?' (group suggestion only)':''}</span><span class="badge">${r.count_group<0?r.count_status:'C'+r.count_group+' · '+r.count_status}</span><span class="badge">${r.residual_count_group<0?'R unassigned':'R'+r.residual_count_group+' · '+r.residual_count_status}</span><span class="badge">${r.joint_group<0?'J unassigned':'J'+r.joint_group}</span><br>${safe(r.group_description)}<br><span class="badge">${safe(r.encounter_tag)}</span><span class="badge">${safe(expertLabel(r))}</span> · perihelion ${safe(r.encounter_perihelion_date||'unassigned')}<br><b>${num(r.solar_distance_Rs,4)} R☉ · ${num(r.solar_distance_AU,4)} AU · ${r.radial_direction}</b><br>PC1 ${num(r.pc1,5)} · PC2 ${num(r.pc2,5)} (dimensionless scores)<br>Analog silhouette ${num(r.silhouette)} · resample agreement ${num(r.stability)} · geometric-mean electric crest ${num(r.impulsiveness)}<br>Counts ${r.counts_present===false?'channel absent':r.counts_total.toLocaleString()} · time since sweep start ${num(r.SWEAP_Start,6)} s · fitted count scale ${num(r.counts_phase_gain)} · raw-count agreement ${num(r.count_stability)}<br>Supported matching-status phase baseline: ${r.counts_phase_baseline_status_matched?'yes':'unavailable; cross-status preview only'}<br><b>SCM flags: ${safe(r.scm_voltage_flags)}</b><br>Max SCM coherence outside lines ${num(r.scm_voltage_max_outside_line_coherence)} · max envelope |r| ${num(r.scm_voltage_max_envelope_abs_r)}<br>Peak voltage/count residual r ${num(r.voltage_count_peak_r)} · ${safe(r.voltage_count_peak_trace)} · counts lag ${num(r.voltage_count_peak_lag_ms)} ms (selected across traces/lags)<br>Selection: ${r.Burst_Type_Name} · trigger ${r.Trigger_Source_Name} · SWEAP status ${r.SWEAP_Status} · TWTA flag ${r.SC_TWTA_On_Flag}<br><span class="muted">${safe(r.file)} · record ${r.record} · burst ID ${r.Burst_ID} · TT2000 ${r.tt2000}</span>`;let fig=DATA.examples[current];$('figure').style.display=fig?'inline':'none';if(fig)$('figure').href=fig;let unitmode=$('scale').value,fs=r.Sample_Speed,n=r.N_Samples_per_Channel;let tx=Array.from({length:256},(_,k)=>(k+.5)*n/256/fs*1000),tz=Array.from({length:512},(_,k)=>(p.zoom_start+k)/fs*1000),fx=p.freq.map(f=>f/1000);for(let j=0;j<5;j++){let channel=p.channels[j];if(!channel){for(let col=0;col<3;col++)chart($(`plot${j}${col}`),tx,[],'Channel absent','ms','');continue}let unit=j===4?'nT':'mV',div=unitmode==='rms'?p.rms[j]:1;if(unitmode==='rms')unit='RMS units';chart($(`plot${j}0`),tx,[],channel,'ms',unit,false,{lo:p.lo[j].map(v=>v/div),hi:p.hi[j].map(v=>v/div),color:colors[j]});chart($(`plot${j}1`),tz,[{y:p.zoom[j].map(v=>v/div),color:colors[j]}],channel,'ms',unit);chart($(`plot${j}2`),fx,[{y:p.psd_db[j],color:colors[j]}],channel,'kHz',j===4?'dB nT²/Hz':'dB mV²/Hz',true)}chart($('plot50'),tx,[{y:p.counts.bins,color:'#222',step:true},{y:p.counts.phase_expected,color:'#d86b25',width:1.2}],'SPAN-e','ms','counts/bin');chart($('plot51'),tz,[{y:p.counts.zoom,color:'#222',step:true}],'SPAN-e','ms','counts/sample');chart($('plot52'),fx,r.counts_total?[{y:p.counts.psd_db,color:'#222'}]:[],'SPAN-e'+(r.counts_total?'':' · zero counts'),'kHz','dB counts²/Hz',true);chart($('residual'),tx,[{y:p.counts.phase_residual,color:'#495d8b'}],'SPAN-e departures from scaled scan reference','ms','standardized residual');if(r.counts_present===false){for(let col=0;col<3;col++)chart($(`plot5${col}`),tx,[],'SPAN-e channel absent','ms','');chart($('residual'),tx,[],'No electron-count data','ms','')}let a=annotations[r.event]||{};$('label').value=a.label||'';$('notes').value=a.notes||'';$('saved').textContent=a.saved?'Last saved '+a.saved:'Notes are stored in this browser. Export them to preserve a portable copy.';$('scmpairs').innerHTML=(DATA.scm_pairs[r.event]||[]).length?'<table><thead><tr><th>Pair</th><th>Native r</th><th>Envelope r₀</th><th>Envelope peak r / lag ms</th><th>Raw coherence</th><th>Outside-line coherence</th><th>Outside-line peak kHz</th><th>Flags</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+(DATA.scm_pairs[r.event]||[]).map(v=>`<tr><td>${safe(v.voltage)} / ${safe(v.scm)}</td><td>${num(v.native_r0)}</td><td>${num(v.envelope_r0)}</td><td>${num(v.envelope_peak_r)} / ${num(v.scm_lag_ms)}</td><td>${num(v.weighted_coherence_raw)}</td><td>${num(v.weighted_coherence_outside_lines)}</td><td>${num(v.peak_coherence_frequency_hz/1000)}</td><td>${safe(v.flags)}</td></tr>`).join('')+'</tbody></table>':'Not assessed: saturation or missing SCM.';renderList();drawMap();neighbors(r)}
function neighbors(r){if(r.group<0){$('neighbors').textContent='Not compared: different or incomplete analog configuration.';return}let m=DATA.model;let center=m.scaling_median,scale=m.scaling_iqr,keys=m.feature_names,fx=DATA.features;if(!fx){$('neighbors').textContent='Use adjacent points in the map or group filters.';return}let z=fx[r.event];let ds=fx.map((v,i)=>[v.reduce((s,a,j)=>s+(a-z[j])**2,0),i]).filter(v=>v[1]!==r.event&&rows[v[1]].group>=0).sort((a,b)=>a[0]-b[0]).slice(0,6);$('neighbors').innerHTML=ds.map(v=>`<button data-pick="${v[1]}">Event ${v[1]} · G${rows[v[1]].group}</button>`).join(' ')}
async function init(){try{let bin=Uint8Array.from(atob($('payload').textContent.trim()),c=>c.charCodeAt(0));let decompressed=new Blob([bin]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip'));DATA=JSON.parse(await new Response(decompressed).text());rows=DATA.rows;previews=DATA.p;try{annotations=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('psp-tds-review-v1')||'{}')}catch{};$('groups').innerHTML=DATA.model.groups.map(g=>`<div class="card" style="border-top-color:${colors[g.group]}"><h3>G${g.group} · ${g.n} records</h3><p>${safe(DATA.names[g.group])}</p><p class="muted">${g.core} core · median agreement ${num(g.median_stability)}</p><button data-pick="${g.medoid}">Inspect medoid ${g.medoid}</button></div>`).join('');$('agroup').innerHTML+=DATA.alternate.groups.map(g=>`<option value="${g.group}">A${g.group}</option>`).join('');$('group').innerHTML+='<option value="-1">Unassigned configuration</option>';$('group').innerHTML+=DATA.model.groups.map(g=>`<option value="${g.group}">G${g.group}: ${safe(DATA.names[g.group])}</option>`).join('');for(let j=0;j<6;j++)for(let k=0;k<3;k++){let c=document.createElement('canvas');c.id=`plot${j}${k}`;c.className='chart';$('plots').appendChild(c)}$('app').style.display='block';$('loading').style.display='none';for(let id of ['encounter','scmflag','group','agroup','status','cgroup','day','radius','leg','sort'])$(id).addEventListener('change',filter);$('search').addEventListener('input',filter);$('cview').addEventListener('change',populateCountFilter);$('scale').addEventListener('change',()=>select(current));$('clear').onclick=()=>{['encounter','scmflag','group','agroup','status','cgroup','day','radius','leg','search'].forEach(id=>$(id).value='');$('sort').value='time';filter()};$('events').onclick=e=>{let tr=e.target.closest('[data-id]');if(tr)select(tr.dataset.id)};document.addEventListener('click',e=>{let b=e.target.closest('[data-pick]');if(b){select(b.dataset.pick);$('explorer').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'})}});$('next').onclick=()=>step(1);$('previous').onclick=()=>step(-1);$('map').onclick=e=>{let b=$('map').getBoundingClientRect(),x=e.clientX-b.left,y=e.clientY-b.top;let hit=mapped.map(p=>[(p[0]-x)**2+(p[1]-y)**2,p[2]]).sort((a,b)=>a[0]-b[0])[0];if(hit)select(hit[1])};$('save').onclick=()=>{annotations[current]={event:current,file:rows[current].file,record:rows[current].record,utc:rows[current].utc,label:$('label').value,notes:$('notes').value,saved:new Date().toISOString()};try{localStorage.setItem('psp-tds-review-v1',JSON.stringify(annotations));$('saved').textContent='Saved in this browser.'}catch{$('saved').textContent='Saved in memory only. Export annotations before closing.'}};$('export').onclick=()=>{let a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(Object.values(annotations),null,2)],{type:'application/json'}));a.download='tds_review_annotations.json';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href),1000)};window.addEventListener('resize',()=>select(current));populateCountFilter();select(601);window.atlasReady=true;}catch(e){$('loading').innerHTML='Unable to load previews: '+safe(e.message)+'<p>Open in a current browser with DecompressionStream support.</p>';window.atlasError=String(e)}}
function step(d){let i=filtered.findIndex(r=>r.event===current);if(filtered.length)select(filtered[(i+d+filtered.length)%filtered.length].event)}
init();
</script></body></html>
